Description: Engaging the private sector in contraceptive method supply is
    critical for equitable, sustainable, and accessible healthcare systems.
    This package implements Bayesian hierarchical models to estimate public
    and private contraceptive supply shares over time at national and
    subnational levels, using Demographic and Health Survey (DHS) data.
    Penalized splines are used to track supply shares over time, and spatial
    correlation structures link national and subnational estimates in data-
    sparse settings.
